      "rationale": "Nominal TRAIN OOF thresholds derived at B=0.20 caused realized FWR to inflate to 0.3000 on DEV_CAL and 0.2922 on DEV_SEARCH due to acoustic distribution shift across non-native L2 accents. Budget B=0.12 (allocating 0.02 S, 0.08 O, 0.02 I on TRAIN OOF) was chosen after observing DEV performance as the required acoustic scale factor to achieve realized FWR <= 0.20 (0.1867 on DEV_CAL, 0.1853 on DEV_SEARCH). This choice is explicitly disclosed and pre-registered here to preclude retrospective threshold selection on TEST labels."
